## Surprises & infra gaps

1. **Placeholder mismatch** — single root cause of ~80 fails. Fixtures hadn't been updated when the unified search dialog landed. Easy to miss without running the actual fixture-level locator.
2. **Phase-0 fetch refactor caused worker teardown** — moving `fetch()` from `mainWindow.evaluate()` (renderer) to Playwright Node context hung the worker on teardown. Surprising; on phase-0 this works because of separate transport layer. Had to revert.
3. **`isSearching` gates filter buttons** — phase-0's `openFilesSearch` helper clicked a `Files` button right after opening the search dialog, but filter buttons only render once query is non-empty. Phase-0 didn't notice because their flow was different.
4. **Phase-0 deleted 3 spec files** (96/97/98 tree-view + 87 agent-lock + 40/41 hooks). Kept them on main.
5. **`window.api.tags.createTag` exists** but `slayzone:tag-created` custom event listener does NOT — would need additional renderer changes to make phase-0's 12-tags second-test workaround actually work.
6. **Test pace ~25-30/min normal, ~6/min in `git/93-resume-command` cluster** (10s timeouts each). That cluster alone takes 3+ min.
7. **SLAYZONE_DB_DIR vs SLAYZONE_STORE_DIR**: main still uses DB_DIR despite plan briefing slice-1 had renamed it. Aligned all fixtures to current main state.

